## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical React Native list rendering and performance basics on mid-range devices.

## Key Concepts

- FlatList virtualization and windowing
- getItemLayout for stable item heights
- keyExtractor for stable keys
- memoization to prevent re-renders
- image loading with caching and placeholders

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal FlatList usage sketch
const RestaurantCard = React.memo(({item}) => (
  <View style={styles.card}>
    <Image source={{uri: item.image}} style={styles.thumb} />
    <Text>{item.name}</Text>
  </View>
));
<FlatList
  data={restaurants}
  renderItem={({item}) => <RestaurantCard item={item} />}
  keyExtractor={item => item.id}
  getItemLayout={(_, index) => ({length: 100, offset: 100 * index, index})}
  initialNumToRender={10}
  windowSize={21}
  removeClippedSubviews
/>
```

