## Why This Is Asked
Tests designing a robust offline-first data store with CRDTs, native modules, and careful backpressure for React Native UIs, plus encryption and delta synchronization considerations.

## Key Concepts
- CRDTs: OR-Set for fields, RGA for ordered lists; per-record envelopes
- Delta-based synchronization and backpressure control
- JSI/TurboModule bridging; AES-GCM encryption at rest
- Conflict resolution: per-field last-writer-wins with server tie-breaker
- Failure modes: partial synchronization, divergence, encryption/key rotation

## Code Example
```javascript
// RN usage sketch
import {NativeCRDTStore} from 'react-native-crdt-store';

const store = new NativeCRDTStore({
  encryptionKey: 'base64-key',
  syncEndpoint: 'https://api.example.com/sync'
});

// Create inspection record
const report = await store.create('inspection', {
  technicianId: 'tech_123',
  timestamp: Date.now(),
  items: ['item1', 'item2'] // RGA for ordered items
});

// Offline updates automatically merge
await store.update(report.id, {
  status: 'completed',
  notes: 'Inspection finished'
});

// Sync with backpressure awareness
store.startSync({
  batchSize: 100,
  maxConcurrency: 3
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, cross‑platform ML bridge, handle memory budgets, dynamic model loading, and a React hook API that cleanly abstracts native work.

## Key Concepts
- React Native bridging and native modules
- Cross‑platform ML inference (TFLite/Core ML)
- Dynamic model loading and versioning
- Concurrency, worker threads, and input backpressure
- Memory budgeting and lifecycle management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal hook sketch (conceptual)
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { NativeModules } from 'react-native';
const { MLBridge } = NativeModules;

export function useMLInference(modelName, inputs) {
  const [pred, setPred] = useState(null);
  const queue = useRef([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!inputs) return;
    queue.current.push(inputs);
    MLBridge.enqueue(modelName, inputs)
      .then(result => setPred(result))
      .catch(() => {});
  }, [modelName, inputs]);

  return pred;
}
```

